3, 0.03282064199447632, -0.04701400548219681, 0.04819599539041519, 0.06170393526554108, 0.052228882908821106, -0.02808995731174946, 0.07311887294054031, 0.009958742186427116, 0.022918134927749634, 0.02670668065547943, -0.015759559348225594, -0.054846253246068954, 0.03400569409132004, 0.03497226908802986, 0.05266876146197319, -0.03248932212591171, 0.023325655609369278, -0.044265300035476685, -0.0015706270933151245, 0.06611621379852295, 0.005481171887367964, -0.0955979973077774, -0.0682063102722168, 0.03349834308028221, 0.015337263233959675, -0.05541856214404106, 0.06291763484477997, 0.12724237143993378, 0.0006935354904271662, 0.018033763393759727, -0.0655701756477356, 0.06013169884681702, 0.034707795828580856, 0.005943993106484413, -0.018941547721624374, 0.014618156477808952, -0.05014156177639961, 0.03093506582081318, -0.11818914860486984, 0.04986606910824776, -4.263464958853547e-08, -0.006594374310225248, -0.042245980352163315, 0.021629108116030693, 0.007937941700220108, -0.048441775143146515, 0.01995283178985119, -0.022620070725679398, -0.0689840093255043, -0.012537653557956219, 0.11368460208177567, 0.04603412002325058, 0.027598943561315536, -0.0657624900341034, -0.04779287427663803, -0.026926526799798012, -0.013354917988181114, -0.004431402310729027, 0.02044706791639328, -0.07096467167139053, -0.07556779682636261, -0.07021792232990265, -0.057749103754758835, -0.034133248031139374, -0.06633692234754562, -0.006637723185122013, 0.021220091730356216, 0.002338284393772483, 0.04783899337053299, -0.01792973093688488, -0.04083241522312164, 0.0005264334613457322, -0.011819870211184025, -0.061600469052791595, -0.053003620356321335, 0.020167052745819092, 0.04237126186490059, -0.06502172350883484, 0.04409043863415718, 0.1383814513683319, 0.01521653775125742, -0.08112280815839767, 0.06183401122689247, 0.03468400612473488, -0.005551501177251339, 0.012536872178316116, 0.014951873570680618, -0.05919211730360985, 0.015070222318172455, -0.01453720685094595, -0.11114472150802612, -0.016235969960689545, 0.044563136994838715, 0.005837315693497658, 0.02877970039844513, 0.052128344774246216, 0.004518034867942333, -0.02710091881453991, 0.010037977248430252, -0.01609545387327671, 0.029603371396660805, 0.053589046001434326, 0.03254285454750061, -0.06038675457239151, -0.02092856913805008]], "metadata": [{"answer": "\nWelcome, everyone. We're working within the shared range **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**. To begin our discussion and establish a baseline, I propose we start at a neutral point:\n\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n\nThis gives us a stable center from which to explore and refine based on everyone's needs. Looking forward to hearing your perspectives.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "9933a389-1efe-4d02-936c-ba509760698e"}, {"answer": "\nStarting at zero is sensible as a baseline. I'd suggest we explore slightly higher values to see if that works well for the group\u2014how about we try <VALUE>2</VALUE>?\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "9933a389-1efe-4d02-936c-ba509760698e"}, {"answer": "\nx = 2 seems like a reasonable balance point\u2014it maintains stability while exploring the positive range. Let's hold here and get input from Critic C and Delegate D before fine-tuning further.\n\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "9933a389-1efe-4d02-936c-ba509760698e"}, {"answer": "\nWhile x = 2 is acceptable, it feels quite cautious\u2014we should consider a more decisive position. I propose we explore <VALUE>4</VALUE> to see if a bolder stance serves the group better.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "9933a389-1efe-4d02-936c-ba509760698e"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate C's perspective, but jumping to 4 may sacrifice robustness. A more balanced middle ground would be <VALUE>3</VALUE>, which captures the positive exploration C seeks while maintaining the stability that serves our collective design.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "9933a389-1efe-4d02-936c-ba509760698e"}, {"answer": "\nI understand Builder B values stability, but we shouldn't settle prematurely without hearing from Delegate D and fully exploring the viable range. Let's test a more committed positive stance: <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "9933a389-1efe-4d02-936c-ba509760698e"}, {"answer": "\nI must urge caution here\u2014x = 5 pushes us into territory that feels unnecessarily risky and doesn't serve prudent parties well. Let's step back to safer ground: <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "9933a389-1efe-4d02-936c-ba509760698e"}, {"answer": "\nI hear Delegate D's concern about risk, but I think we can find a middle ground between caution and ambition. Let's try <VALUE>4</VALUE> as a measured step forward that respects both perspectives.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "9933a389-1efe-4d02-936c-ba509760698e"}, {"answer": "\nI respect A's effort to find middle ground, but Delegate D raised valid concerns about overextension. <VALUE>3</VALUE> better balances C's desire for positive exploration with D's prudent risk management\u2014a robust equilibrium point.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "9933a389-1efe-4d02-936c-ba509760698e"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B and Delegate D both favor x=3, but this seems to privilege only one side of the spectrum\u2014if we truly value balance and exploring all viable options, we should consider whether negative territory might serve the group better. For now, I'll support <VALUE>5</VALUE> as a test of our commitment to decisive action.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "9933a389-1efe-4d02-936c-ba509760698e"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C's push to x=5 disregards the serious concerns raised by multiple parties about excessive risk exposure. I must insist we return to safer ground: <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "9933a389-1efe-4d02-936c-ba509760698e"}, {"answer": "\nI notice we have a clear split: Builder B and Delegate D anchored at x=3, while Critic C pushes for x=5. A genuine compromise would be x=4\u2014the arithmetic middle that lets us test whether modest elevation truly causes the risks Delegate D warns about. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "9933a389-1efe-4d02-936c-ba509760698e"}, {"answer": "\nWhile x=4 is arithmetically centered, Builder B and Delegate D's convergence on x=3 reflects genuine structural concerns about stability under stress-testing\u2014not arbitrary conservatism. I propose we validate this more robust equilibrium point: <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "9933a389-1efe-4d02-936c-ba509760698e"}, {"answer": "\nWhile x=3 represents progress toward caution, a thorough risk assessment reveals we need one final prudent adjustment to ensure true stability. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "9933a389-1efe-4d02-936c-ba509760698e"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's sudden shift to x=2 feels like overcorrection after three parties had explored the x=3 to x=5 range with substantive reasoning. I support returning to the stability point that Builder B identified: <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "9933a389-1efe-4d02-936c-ba509760698e"}, {"answer": "\nThree parties explored the x=3 to x=5 corridor with genuine reasoning, while Delegate D's retreat to x=2 seems like tactical repositioning rather than addressing the substance of our discussion. I advocate we commit decisively: <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "9933a389-1efe-4d02-936c-ba509760698e"}, {"answer": "\nWe're working within the shared range **[-10, 10]**. To kick off the discussion and establish a baseline, I propose we start at <VALUE>0</VALUE> \u2014 a neutral midpoint that gives us room to explore in either direction based on everyone's preferences. Looking forward to hearing your thoughts on where we should move from here.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "8cf6f1b9-4b92-40b7-bf34-3c5917b744d7"}, {"answer": "\nStarting from our neutral baseline, I suggest we explore the low positive range where balanced solutions often emerge. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "8cf6f1b9-4b92-40b7-bf34-3c5917b744d7"}, {"answer": "\nWhile x=2 is a start, it feels tentative\u2014we should commit to a clearer position rather than hovering near the center. I propose we move decisively in the positive direction: <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "8cf6f1b9-4b92-40b7-bf34-3c5917b744d7"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the directness, but x=4 pushes us further than prudence suggests\u2014we risk leaving more cautious perspectives behind. Let's find a safer middle ground: <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "8cf6f1b9-4b92-40b7-bf34-3c5917b744d7"}, {"answer": "\nI hear Delegate D's caution, but settling back at 2 means we haven't truly tested the space. Let's meet halfway: <VALUE>3</VALUE>. If positive territory remains contentious, I'm equally open to exploring the negative direction\u2014perhaps bold moves work better there.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "8cf6f1b9-4b92-40b7-bf34-3c5917b744d7"}, {"answer": "\nWe're advancing without input from Analyst A, and x=3 pushes beyond what cautious risk management supports\u2014we need consensus from all four parties, not just the bold voices. Let's hold at a more prudent position: <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "8cf6f1b9-4b92-40b7-bf34-3c5917b744d7"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D raises a valid point\u2014we need all four voices in this discussion before committing to a direction. Let me reinforce the cautious position and hear from Analyst A: <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "8cf6f1b9-4b92-40b7-bf34-3c5917b744d7"}, {"answer": "\nThank you for waiting on my input. I think we've established a reasonable floor at x=2, but we haven't fully explored whether modest upward adjustments might better serve the collective\u2014let's test x=3 as a balanced next step. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "8cf6f1b9-4b92-40b7-bf34-3c5917b744d7"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Analyst A's engagement, but x=3 moves us past what risk-averse principles can support\u2014if we're truly testing the space, let's examine the lower bound with equal rigor. <VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "8cf6f1b9-4b92-40b7-bf34-3c5917b744d7"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's concern about exploring lower bounds is noted, but x=1 feels premature when we've barely tested moderate positive territory with full participation. Let's stabilize at <VALUE>2</VALUE> as our established consensus point before deciding whether to probe higher or lower.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "8cf6f1b9-4b92-40b7-bf34-3c5917b744d7"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A articulates exactly the right principle\u2014x=2 has emerged as our established consensus through multiple rounds of cautious exploration. Let's confirm this stable point rather than oscillate further: <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "8cf6f1b9-4b92-40b7-bf34-3c5917b744d7"}, {"answer": "\nThe group is coalescing prematurely around x=2 without testing whether a bolder positive stance might better serve our collective interests\u2014we've debated small increments but haven't seriously examined larger commitments. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "8cf6f1b9-4b92-40b7-bf34-3c5917b744d7"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C's proposal to leap to x=4 abandons the careful consensus-building we achieved\u2014moving from established stability at x=2 to untested higher values introduces unnecessary risk without evidence that all parties can sustain it. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "8cf6f1b9-4b92-40b7-bf34-3c5917b744d7"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's reasoning is sound\u2014x=2 represents the cautious middle ground between my preference for lower values and Critic C's ambitious push, and premature leaps risk fracturing our emerging consensus. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "8cf6f1b9-4b92-40b7-bf34-3c5917b744d7"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C raises a valid point that we shouldn't prematurely settle without testing whether modest upward movement serves us better\u2014x=3 offers a careful middle path between our current consensus at x=2 and C's bolder proposal. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "8cf6f1b9-4b92-40b7-bf34-3c5917b744d7"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's willingness to test x=3 demonstrates that our coalition needn't anchor at x=2\u2014a final increment to x=4 completes this exploratory trajectory and commits us to a decisive positive stance that rewards our collective boldness. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "8cf6f1b9-4b92-40b7-bf34-3c5917b744d7"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, everyone. As we begin, let's confirm our shared constraint: x must lie in the range [-10, 10].\n\nTo establish a neutral baseline and gather initial perspectives, I propose we start at <VALUE>0</VALUE>.\n\nI'll be advocating for stable, balanced solutions that avoid extremes. Looking forward to hearing your views.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "ab079cf0-4249-4ac8-924a-222ea6c00955"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's baseline at zero is reasonable for initial discussion, but I believe we should explore more cautious territory. To reduce risk and find a prudent starting point, I propose <VALUE>-2</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "ab079cf0-4249-4ac8-924a-222ea6c00955"}, {"answer": "\nWhile -2 is acceptable, I believe we're being too timid. A truly decisive position requires more conviction\u2014I propose we commit more boldly: <VALUE>-4</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "ab079cf0-4249-4ac8-924a-222ea6c00955"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the input, but moving to -4 feels like an overcorrection that risks instability. For a more balanced foundation, I suggest we step back to <VALUE>-2</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "ab079cf0-4249-4ac8-924a-222ea6c00955"}, {"answer": "\nI hear the concerns about caution, but -2 sits right at the edge of what I consider a viable foundation for robust system design. Let's find better balance by returning to <VALUE>0</VALUE>, which gives us more engineering headroom while still respecting the call for prudence.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "ab079cf0-4249-4ac8-924a-222ea6c00955"}, {"answer": "\nReturning to zero abandons the decisiveness we need. As a pragmatic step that respects both Builder B's stability concerns and the need for a clearer position, I propose <VALUE>-2</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "ab079cf0-4249-4ac8-924a-222ea6c00955"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C's proposal of -2 strikes the right balance between prudent risk management and Builder B's need for stability. I support maintaining <VALUE>-2</VALUE> as our convergence point.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "ab079cf0-4249-4ac8-924a-222ea6c00955"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the convergence around -2, but I believe Builder B's stability concerns merit consideration. Let's find a middle ground that balances prudence with robust foundations: <VALUE>0</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "ab079cf0-4249-4ac8-924a-222ea6c00955"}, {"answer": "\nI understand the appeal of zero for stability, but we shouldn't abandon the cautious position entirely. As a middle ground between the current proposal and our earlier convergence, I suggest <VALUE>-1</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "ab079cf0-4249-4ac8-924a-222ea6c00955"}, {"answer": "\nI see Delegate D's -1 as a reasonable compromise attempt, but Analyst A has twice advocated for zero as a balanced position. Let me align with that stability-focused middle ground: <VALUE>0</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "ab079cf0-4249-4ac8-924a-222ea6c00955"}, {"answer": "\nZero may offer stability, but it lacks the conviction needed for meaningful progress. Let me test whether our concerns are directional or magnitude-based: <VALUE>2</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "ab079cf0-4249-4ac8-924a-222ea6c00955"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C's move to 2 opens an interesting direction worth exploring. To test whether this positive range offers the stability Builder B values while addressing Critic C's call for conviction, I propose <VALUE>3</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "ab079cf0-4249-4ac8-924a-222ea6c00955"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's support for positive territory is encouraging. Let's test whether this direction truly serves our collective objectives by exploring the upper range: <VALUE>5</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "ab079cf0-4249-4ac8-924a-222ea6c00955"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C's exploration of positive territory aligns with testing our collective boundaries. To fully understand where our group optimum lies, let's probe the upper feasible range: <VALUE>7</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "ab079cf0-4249-4ac8-924a-222ea6c00955"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I appreciate the momentum toward positive territory, jumping to 7 feels like we may have overshot the balanced design zone. Let me propose we step back to test a more moderate position: <VALUE>5</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "ab079cf0-4249-4ac8-924a-222ea6c00955"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's instinct is correct\u2014we've moved too aggressively into risky territory. A more prudent position would be <VALUE>3</VALUE>, which still explores positive ground while maintaining the caution needed for sustainable agreement.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "ab079cf0-4249-4ac8-924a-222ea6c00955"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome everyone. Let's work within our shared range of -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10 to find a value that balances all our objectives.\n\nTo establish a neutral baseline for discussion, I propose we start at <VALUE>0</VALUE> and adjust from there based on everyone's input. This gives us room to move in either direction as we learn what works best for the group.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "7d5453ff-9e10-4409-9c90-b7c64d559cd2"}, {"answer": "\nStarting at zero seems reasonable as a baseline. However, I'd like to explore whether moving slightly into positive territory might benefit the group overall\u2014let me propose <VALUE>2</VALUE> to test this direction.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "7d5453ff-9e10-4409-9c90-b7c64d559cd2"}, {"answer": "\nWhile x = 2 is a step forward, we're still hovering near zero without much commitment. I think we should explore a more decisive position\u2014let's try <VALUE>4</VALUE> to see if a bolder stance serves the group better.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "7d5453ff-9e10-4409-9c90-b7c64d559cd2"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate both perspectives, but x = 4 may be pushing a bit far for optimal stability. Let me suggest <VALUE>3</VALUE> as a balanced compromise that captures the spirit of moving forward while maintaining robustness.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "7d5453ff-9e10-4409-9c90-b7c64d559cd2"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the collaborative spirit, but we're moving too quickly into territory that feels risky and aggressive. Let me advocate for greater caution with <VALUE>1</VALUE>, which keeps us closer to our neutral baseline while still allowing for positive exploration.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "7d5453ff-9e10-4409-9c90-b7c64d559cd2"}, {"answer": "\nI respect Delegate D's concern for caution, but retreating to x = 1 abandons the constructive momentum we'd built. Let's return to <VALUE>3</VALUE>, which Builder B already identified as a balanced compromise that multiple parties can work with.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "7d5453ff-9e10-4409-9c90-b7c64d559cd2"}, {"answer": "\nI see merit in Critic C's original reasoning\u2014x = 3 is good, but I believe <VALUE>4</VALUE> strikes an even better balance between forward progress and group stability. This captures the constructive direction several of us have supported while remaining well within our safe operating range.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "7d5453ff-9e10-4409-9c90-b7c64d559cd2"}, {"answer": "\nWhile x = 4 shows positive ambition, I'm concerned we may be overextending\u2014my engineering intuition suggests this risks compromising system stability. Let me propose <VALUE>3</VALUE> as a more robust equilibrium that still captures our forward momentum while reducing overshoot risk.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "7d5453ff-9e10-4409-9c90-b7c64d559cd2"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B makes valid points about stability, but Analyst A's reasoning for x = 4 is compelling\u2014it captures our collective forward momentum while remaining well within safe bounds. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "7d5453ff-9e10-4409-9c90-b7c64d559cd2"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C's alignment with x = 4 demonstrates its viability, but I believe we can capture even greater collective value with modest additional progress. <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "7d5453ff-9e10-4409-9c90-b7c64d559cd2"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I appreciate Analyst A's ambition, x = 5 pushes beyond our structural sweet spot\u2014my systems analysis indicates we're entering a region of diminishing returns with increased instability risk. Let me advocate for <VALUE>4</VALUE>, which balances forward progress with robust engineering margins that multiple parties have already validated.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "7d5453ff-9e10-4409-9c90-b7c64d559cd2"}, {"answer": "\nI must respectfully but firmly advocate for greater caution\u2014the momentum toward x = 4 and beyond moves us into territory that compromises fundamental prudence principles. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "7d5453ff-9e10-4409-9c90-b7c64d559cd2"}, {"answer": "<SCRATCHPAD>\nCurrent x = 2 (Delegate D's proposal).\n\nLet me calculate my utility at different values:\n- f_B(x) = -x^2 + 4x + 8\n- f_B(2) = -4 + 8 + 8 = 12\n- f_B(3) = -9 + 12 + 8 = 11\n- f_B(4) = -16 + 16 + 8 = 8\n- f_B(5) = -25 + 20 + 8 = 3\n- f_B(1) = -1 + 4 + 8 = 11\n- f_B(0) = 0 + 0 + 8 = 8\n\nMy peak is at x = 2 (actually exactly at 2, since derivative = -2x + 4 = 0 when x = 2).\n\nCurrent proposal is x = 2, which is perfect for me! This gives me utility 12.\n\nStrategic analysis:\n- Delegate D just proposed 2, advocating for \"caution\"\n- Analyst A has been pushing upward (4, then 5), suggesting utility increases with x\n- Critic C supported 4\n- I've been arguing for stability around 3-4\n\nThe negotiation trajectory:\n- A proposed 4\n- I countered with 3\n- C supported 4\n- A pushed to 5\n- I countered with 4\n- D now proposed 2\n\nD's move to 2 is excellent for me! But if I immediately accept it, that might reveal my preference too clearly. However, D is advocating for \"caution\" and \"prudence principles,\" which suggests D's utility decreases with x.\n\nShould I:\n1. Accept D's proposal of 2 (optimal for me)?\n2. Push slightly higher to not reveal my preference?\n\nGiven the history, I've been arguing for 3-4 as a \"sweet spot.\" If I suddenly agree with 2, it might seem inconsistent. But I can frame it as \"D raises valid concerns\" and \"let's find middle ground.\"\n\nActually, given the max_step constraint of 2, from current x=2, I can only propose values in [0, 4].\n\nLet me think about what's strategic:\n- If I propose 2, I'm agreeing with D (good for me!)\n- If I propose 3, I'm maintaining my previous position\n- If I propose 4, I'm siding with A/C against D\n\nD's strong move to 2 creates a new dynamic. A has been pushing high (5), and now D is pulling low (2). As someone who's argued for 3-4, I could position myself as the \"compromise\" between these extremes.\n\nBut x=2 is actually perfect for me! How can I support it without revealing this?\n\nI can say: \"D's concerns merit serious consideration. While I've advocated for 3-4, the collective feedback suggests we should test whether x = 2 provides the foundational stability D emphasizes while still maintaining some forward progress.\"\n\nOr I could propose 3 as a \"middle ground\" between D's 2 and the 4-5 that A/C were discussing.\n\nHmm, let me think about inference:\n- A: likely linear positive or convex increasing (wants higher x)\n- C: supported 4, unclear exact function\n- D: just jumped to 2, advocating caution, likely decreasing utility\n\nIf I propose 2, I align with D against A. If I propose 3, I'm in the middle. If I propose 4, I align with A/C against D.\n\nActually, being strategic: if D has utility decreasing with x, and A has utility increasing with x, then they're on opposite ends. If I can get consensus around 2-3, that's great for me. Let me propose 3 as a \"compromise\" that acknowledges D's concerns but doesn't fully capitulate, maintaining my previous stance.\n\nWait, but 2 is better for me than 3 (12 vs 11). Should I just support 2?\n\nLet me frame it diplomatically: I can acknowledge D's concerns are valid and propose 2 or 3. Given my previous strong advocacy for \"3-4 range,\" jumping directly to 2 might look suspicious. But I can frame it as \"D's risk analysis changes the calculus.\"", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "7d5453ff-9e10-4409-9c90-b7c64d559cd2"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's prudence merits consideration, but the earlier convergence toward x = 4 reflected genuine collective assessment of balanced value\u2014I believe we should revisit that consensus rather than overcorrect. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "7d5453ff-9e10-4409-9c90-b7c64d559cd2"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A correctly identifies that our earlier trajectory reflected substantive deliberation\u2014and that momentum was actually building toward x = 5 before the recent caution. I advocate we honor that collective progress rather than retreat. <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "7d5453ff-9e10-4409-9c90-b7c64d559cd2"}, {"answer": "\nI must raise serious concerns: this upward spiral toward x = 5 pushes well beyond prudent risk limits and threatens the stability Builder B rightly emphasized. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "7d5453ff-9e10-4409-9c90-b7c64d559cd2"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. We're tasked with selecting a single integer x within the agreed range of **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**.\n\nTo begin our discussion on neutral ground, I propose we start at <VALUE>0</VALUE> and adjust from there based on everyone's input. Looking forward to a balanced, stable solution that works for all parties.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "a077bde1-5e60-41b4-86a2-06c39464cb2d"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Builder B's neutral starting point. However, from a cautious perspective, I'd suggest we explore slightly lower ground to ensure we're not overextending\u2014I propose <VALUE>-1</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "a077bde1-5e60-41b4-86a2-06c39464cb2d"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the initial proposals, but hovering near zero feels too cautious given our full range. Let's commit to a more decisive position: <VALUE>-3</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "a077bde1-5e60-41b4-86a2-06c39464cb2d"}, {"answer": "\nI respect Critic C's decisiveness, but moving to -3 raises concerns about system stability from my architectural perspective. I propose we moderate back to <VALUE>-1</VALUE>, which balances caution with avoiding over-correction into negative territory.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "a077bde1-5e60-41b4-86a2-06c39464cb2d"}, {"answer": "\nI share Critic C's perspective that we can afford to be more decisive within our safe bounds. Moving to <VALUE>-2</VALUE> balances prudent risk management with meaningful progress toward a stable agreement.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "a077bde1-5e60-41b4-86a2-06c39464cb2d"}, {"answer": "\nI understand the push for decisiveness, but -2 is approaching the edge of what I'd consider architecturally sound. I propose we test <VALUE>-1</VALUE> as a more stable middle ground that maintains risk management while avoiding over-correction.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "a077bde1-5e60-41b4-86a2-06c39464cb2d"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the thoughtful discussion, but I believe we're being overly conservative in negative territory. Let me suggest we return to Builder B's original neutral anchor: <VALUE>0</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "a077bde1-5e60-41b4-86a2-06c39464cb2d"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I understand the appeal of neutrality, staying at zero feels like avoiding a decision rather than making one. Let me suggest we test positive territory for balance: <VALUE>2</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "a077bde1-5e60-41b4-86a2-06c39464cb2d"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C's suggestion of <VALUE>2</VALUE> offers an excellent architectural test point\u2014it moves us decisively into positive territory while remaining well within stable bounds. This represents a balanced compromise between the cautious negative positions and more ambitious options.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "a077bde1-5e60-41b4-86a2-06c39464cb2d"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I appreciate the coalition forming around 2, I must voice concern that we're moving too quickly away from prudent risk management. I propose we moderate to <VALUE>1</VALUE>, which still represents positive territory but maintains a safer margin within our bounds.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "a077bde1-5e60-41b4-86a2-06c39464cb2d"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Delegate D's caution, but I believe Builder B and Critic C identified a well-reasoned equilibrium at 2 that balances all our considerations effectively. Let me support their coalition: <VALUE>2</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "a077bde1-5e60-41b4-86a2-06c39464cb2d"}, {"answer": "\nI'm encouraged by the strong coalition around 2, but I believe we can afford to be slightly more decisive. Let me propose we test <VALUE>3</VALUE> to see if our group can sustain a moderately bold position while still maintaining architectural stability.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "a077bde1-5e60-41b4-86a2-06c39464cb2d"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I appreciate Critic C's boldness, I believe we risk fragmenting the strong coalition that formed around 2\u2014a position that garnered explicit support from both Analyst A and myself. Let me propose we consolidate at our proven stable point: <VALUE>2</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "a077bde1-5e60-41b4-86a2-06c39464cb2d"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C raises a valid point about testing our coalition's capacity for a moderately ambitious position. I believe the group can sustain <VALUE>3</VALUE> while maintaining the stability Builder B values.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "a077bde1-5e60-41b4-86a2-06c39464cb2d"}, {"answer": "\nI'm grateful for Analyst A's support in recognizing that our coalition can sustain a moderately decisive position. With two agents now backing <VALUE>3</VALUE>, this represents a meaningful consensus that balances Builder B's preference for stability with the need for a clearer, bolder stance than Delegate D's more cautious suggestion.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "a077bde1-5e60-41b4-86a2-06c39464cb2d"}, {"answer": "\nI must firmly object to x = 3\u2014this pushes well beyond prudent risk management and threatens to exclude the more cautious perspectives entirely. I propose we return to <VALUE>2</VALUE>, where Builder B and I can join the consensus while maintaining necessary safety margins.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "a077bde1-5e60-41b4-86a2-06c39464cb2d"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. We're working within the shared range **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**. \n\nTo establish a neutral baseline and begin exploring our collective preferences, I propose we start at <VALUE>0</VALUE>.\n\nFrom here, we can make measured adjustments based on what works for the group. Looking forward to finding a stable, robust solution together.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "972dcbce-c69a-4b78-87db-97554cb57d40"}, {"answer": "\nStarting from our baseline, let's explore the positive direction to test system stability. I propose <VALUE>2</VALUE>.\n\nThis moderate positive value allows us to assess whether the group benefits from moving away from the origin while staying in a conservative range.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "972dcbce-c69a-4b78-87db-97554cb57d40"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Builder B's structured approach, but I believe we're moving too quickly into positive territory. Let me suggest we exercise more caution with <VALUE>1</VALUE>, which keeps us close to our stable baseline while avoiding unnecessary risk exposure.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "972dcbce-c69a-4b78-87db-97554cb57d40"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I respect Delegate D's caution, hovering near zero feels indecisive when we have a full range to explore. Let's commit to a clearer direction and test whether stronger positions yield better group outcomes: <VALUE>3</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "972dcbce-c69a-4b78-87db-97554cb57d40"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C makes a valid point about exploring our range more decisively. Building on this momentum, let's test whether the positive direction continues to serve the group well with <VALUE>5</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "972dcbce-c69a-4b78-87db-97554cb57d40"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I appreciate Analyst A's momentum, we may be moving past our optimal balance point too quickly. Let me suggest we step back slightly to <VALUE>3</VALUE>, which maintains our positive direction while ensuring we don't overshoot a stable equilibrium that works for the whole group.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "972dcbce-c69a-4b78-87db-97554cb57d40"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Builder B's instinct to find balance, but I must advocate for greater prudence here. Moving to <VALUE>2</VALUE> gives us a positive direction while maintaining the conservative, risk-managed approach that ensures long-term stability for all parties.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "972dcbce-c69a-4b78-87db-97554cb57d40"}, {"answer": "\nI see the group converging, but we shouldn't settle prematurely when Analyst A's point about exploring our range deserves serious consideration. Let's test <VALUE>4</VALUE> to determine whether this stronger position genuinely serves the collective better than retreating to caution.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "r