ates strongly for 2, A suggested 3 as compromise, and C pushes for 4. The mathematical middle ground and most stable consensus point appears to be <VALUE>3</VALUE>, which represents a balanced position that partially accommodates all perspectives.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "e53bc458-6d31-47b2-b7b2-25a7970cc6ff"}, {"answer": "\nI understand D's concerns, but if we're genuinely committed to the positive direction we've been exploring, we should follow through decisively rather than perpetually retreating. I propose <VALUE>5</VALUE> as a clear, confident position that fully utilizes the reasonable range available to us.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "e53bc458-6d31-47b2-b7b2-25a7970cc6ff"}, {"answer": "\nI find merit in Critic C's confidence, and the data suggests we can indeed explore slightly higher ground safely. I propose <VALUE>6</VALUE> as a position that honors the upward momentum C advocates while remaining measured and within reasonable bounds for all parties.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "e53bc458-6d31-47b2-b7b2-25a7970cc6ff"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I appreciate the exploratory spirit, x=6 pushes beyond the stability margins I can support from an engineering perspective\u2014we're entering territory where system robustness becomes genuinely concerning. I propose we consolidate at <VALUE>4</VALUE>, which C originally advocated and represents a defensible equilibrium point.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "e53bc458-6d31-47b2-b7b2-25a7970cc6ff"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B, I respect your engineering concerns, but I believe x=4 still represents unnecessary caution given that Analyst A has validated the safety of higher ground. I propose <VALUE>5</VALUE> as a position that balances decisive action with prudent risk management.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "e53bc458-6d31-47b2-b7b2-25a7970cc6ff"}, {"answer": "\nI recognize Builder B's engineering concerns are genuine, and Critic C's position at x=5 represents a well-reasoned balance between ambition and prudence. I support <VALUE>5</VALUE> as a stable consensus point that respects both operational safety and forward momentum.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "e53bc458-6d31-47b2-b7b2-25a7970cc6ff"}, {"answer": "\nThe momentum toward x=5 has pushed well beyond prudent risk management boundaries\u2014I must advocate for genuine caution rather than merely symbolic restraint. I propose <VALUE>3</VALUE> as the maximum defensible position that maintains essential safety margins while still respecting the group's desire for positive territory.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "e53bc458-6d31-47b2-b7b2-25a7970cc6ff"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Our shared constraint is clear: -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10.\n\nTo begin our exploration of the solution space, I propose we start from a neutral baseline and adjust incrementally based on everyone's input.\n\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n\nI look forward to understanding what balance works best for our collective objectives.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "f48993d5-96be-43c9-99d4-e178b27ecab9"}, {"answer": "\nStarting from zero seems reasonable as a baseline. However, I believe we might find better mutual value by exploring slightly positive territory.\n\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "f48993d5-96be-43c9-99d4-e178b27ecab9"}, {"answer": "\nWhile 2 is a starting point, I believe we're being too cautious. Let's test whether a more decisive position serves the group better.\n\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "f48993d5-96be-43c9-99d4-e178b27ecab9"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the exploration, but moving to 4 feels too aggressive for a cautious approach. Let's find a more prudent middle ground that balances all perspectives.\n\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Del